### Reviewer Notes

- Certificate is self-signed for development only
- Production deployment requires proper certificates
- All HTTPS configuration uses environment variables
- No hardcoded certificate paths or passwords
- Certificate password configurable via parameter

### Performance Impact

Minimal - HTTPS has <1% overhead in local development. Benefits (security) outweigh costs.

### Security Impact

**Positive:**
- ✅ Communications encrypted in transit
- ✅ Service-to-service calls secured
- ✅ Development environment mirrors production security
- ✅ Certificate management best practices documented

